Subject: [PATCH] static_call: don't re-sort sites that are already sorted

static_call_init() heapsorts .static_call_sites by key on every boot.
Heapsort does O(n log n) compare and swap callbacks even on sorted input,
and each is an indirect call through a retpoline in a mitigated kernel.

Check the order first and sort only if it is wrong. Our build sorts
vmlinux's table (guest/kernel/prepatch.py), so the check is all a boot
pays. An unsorted table (any other build, modules) is sorted as before.

--- a/kernel/static_call_inline.c	2026-10-30 13:06:41.000000000 +0100
+++ b/kernel/static_call_inline.c	2026-11-04 09:47:13.640757545 +0100
@@ -106,6 +106,19 @@
 static inline void static_call_sort_entries(struct static_call_site *start,
 					    struct static_call_site *stop)
 {
+	struct static_call_site *site;
+
+	/*
+	 * The build may have sorted vmlinux's sites already
+	 * (guest/kernel/prepatch.py): a linear check is far cheaper than a
+	 * heapsort, which does O(n log n) indirect calls even on sorted input.
+	 */
+	for (site = start + 1; site < stop; site++)
+		if (static_call_key(site - 1) > static_call_key(site))
+			break;
+	if (site >= stop)
+		return;
+
 	sort(start, stop - start, sizeof(struct static_call_site),
 	     static_call_site_cmp, static_call_site_swap);
 }
